  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the graph of \\(3x + 4y = c\\), where \\(c\\) is a positive constant, crosses the \\(x\\)-axis at point \\(P\\) and the \\(y\\)-axis at point \\(Q\\). The distance between \\(P\\) and \\(Q\\) is 25. What is the value of \\(c\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "60"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(P = \\left(\\frac{c}{3}, 0\\right)\\) and \\(Q = \\left(0, \\frac{c}{4}\\right)\\).",
    "By the Pythagorean theorem, \\(PQ^{2} = \\left(\\frac{c}{3}\\right)^{2} + \\left(\\frac{c}{4}\\right)^{2} = \\frac{25c^{2}}{144}\\), so \\(PQ = \\frac{5c}{12}\\).",
    "Set \\(\\frac{5c}{12} = 25\\): \\(c = 60\\). Check: \\(P = (20, 0)\\), \\(Q = (0, 15)\\), and \\(\\sqrt{20^{2} + 15^{2}} = 25\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "c = symbols('c', positive=True)\nd = sqrt((c/3)**2 + (c/4)**2)\nsol = solve(Eq(d, 25), c)\nassert sol == [60]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
